# Style Rules
- Strong typing, explicit exported fields, concise docstrings for complex functions.
- Clear, meaningful names; avoid cryptic abbreviations.
- Early returns; keep nesting shallow.

# Comments
- Only for non-obvious reasoning, invariants, or caveats. No noise.

# Formatting
- Match local style; prefer multi-line clarity over dense one-liners.

# Linting
- Keep linter clean. Fix integer division warnings explicitly.

## Testing & Validation
- Smoke-test stage flow (spawn → waves → boss) without errors in output.
- Verify pooling: instances are reused, signals disconnected on reuse.
- Confirm bullet caps and rate limits are respected under stress.
- Check CRT/readability shaders after changes; adjust via exported params only.
- Update related configs/docs when behavior changes.